=== Findings

F1 (check 4, blocking). novacore/tests/test_capabilities.py line 10 says
"`test_prompt_catalogue.py` additionally pins that no catalogue entry starts
with `_`". That file does not exist and never has (ls and git log above). The
`_` check is in test_capabilities.py itself
(test_stub_capability_is_absent_from_the_production_boundary). This is the
exact failure AGENTS.md opens with (a comment citing tests/font_ref_test.py).
Line 13, "Covers W4 item 4 n/a, W6 outbox transfer via a patched entry.",
does not say anything a reader can check. Fix: cite the real test, delete or
rewrite line 13.

F2 (check 3, blocking). Break B3 passes the suite. The prompt names
`usb2.mount`, which is not in CATALOGUE, and all 33 tests pass. DOTTED_NAME
is `\b[a-z][a-z_]+\.[a-z][a-z_]+\b`, so a name with a digit is not seen, and
property 2 ("names no capability-like action absent from CATALOGUE") does not
hold for it. Fix: let the pattern accept digits (for example
`\b[a-z][a-z0-9_]+\.[a-z][a-z0-9_]+\b`), show B3 failing, and check that the
current prompt still yields exactly the seven VOCABULARY names. Do not change
VOCABULARY to make anything pass.

F3 (report only, not blocking). Break B4 passes the suite: a prose sentence
"You may power off the machine when asked." promises an action that has no
catalogue entry. A dotted-name regex cannot see prose, and W4 item 4 asks
only for the dotted vocabulary. W4 item 3 lists prose actions of this kind
("power off", "erase/format storage") as the owner's draft-prompt conflict;
that is the owner's decision, not R10's. Put one line in decisions.md or in
the test docstring saying that property 2 covers dotted names only.

F4 (process, not blocking). The R10 commit has no end-of-task block
(WHAT I COULD NOT DO / WHAT I AM UNSURE OF). Post it on the board with the
fixes.

What holds: the four harness probes are caught (re-run above, 4 of 4).
B1 (a confirmation-required name dropped from the prompt), B2 (the network
rule weakened) and B5 (_test.stub back in CATALOGUE) all fail the suite.
_test.stub is out of the production boundary and the tests inject it with
mock.patch.dict. The scope decision is in decisions.md. The trailing newline
removed from SYSTEM_PROMPT changes nothing: its only user,
build_prompt in prompts.py, calls SYSTEM_PROMPT.strip().

Next: the author fixes F1 and F2, re-runs w4, and reports on the board.
The reviewer then re-runs B3 and the w4 harness.

VERDICT: FAIL (F1, F2)
